    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d176">

                <pb facs="0353" n="239" sameAs="frus:frus1924v01/pg239"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.2300/43: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Kellogg</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-02-05T17:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 5,
                                1924—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received February 5—2:57
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>51. Your 10, January 18, 7 p.m.<anchor n="11" xml:id="d176-f1"/> Foreign Office
                    informs me that Canada has granted permission for flight over her territory;
                    will give all facilities asked for.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
